From 206355c9925fe4adc3fcaaee167176051b5c7315 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:12:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/57] hw/arm: generic PIC32CM SoC, PIC32CM1216MC00048 and
 pic32cm-mc00-cpro

The JH01-only SoC becomes pic32cm-soc, an abstract model built from a
generated MchpDeviceInfo descriptor (memory map, instances, IRQ lines,
GCLK channels, NVM rows image, silicon revisions); each device is a
subtype whose descriptor lives in its own translation unit
(hw/arm/<device>.c), because devices with different versions of an IP
define the same register constants differently.

- New device PIC32CM1216MC00048 and board pic32cm-mc00-cpro (EV15N46A):
  12 MHz and 32.768 kHz external oscillators, SERCOM0 (VCOM) and SERCOM3
  on -serial, LED0 on PA24, sw0-pressed for SW0 on PA25.
- Regenerated tables: per-IP constant headers are now shared by both
  devices (merged), register tables are per device under
  include/hw/mchp/gen/<device>/.
- mchp-port and mchp-gclk take their group/channel counts from the
  device's register table (MC00: 2 PORT groups, 35 GCLK channels).
- MchpDeviceInfo and MchpSiliconRev in hw/mchp/mchp_device.h.
- New qtest pic32cm-mc00-test; board documentation.

Peripheral Pretender downstream patch; not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
