new file mode 100644
index 0000000..90651d3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+Microchip PIC32CM MC00 Curiosity Pro (``pic32cm-mc00-cpro``)
+=============================================================
+
+.. note::
+   Peripheral Pretender: a personal project in a downstream fork
+   of QEMU. AI-assisted code; not for submission to upstream QEMU.
+
+The PIC32CM MC00 Curiosity Pro evaluation kit (EV15N46A) carries a
+PIC32CM1216MC00048 microcontroller: an Arm Cortex-M0+ with 128 KiB of
+flash, 4 KiB of data flash and 16 KiB of SRAM, a 12 MHz MEMS oscillator
+on XIN and a 32.768 kHz MEMS oscillator on XIN32 (both external clocks).
+
+The SoC model (``pic32cm1216mc00048-soc``) is the same generic PIC32CM
+model as ``pic32cm5164jh01100-soc`` (see :doc:`pic32cm-jh01-cpro`), built
+from the device description generated from this device's ATDF file and
+profile. Everything said there about the supported devices, their
+limitations, the trace events and the boot options applies here too.
+Peripherals are QOM children of ``/machine/soc`` named after their
+instance (``/machine/soc/sercom0``, ``/machine/soc/port``, ...).
+
+Differences from the PIC32CM JH01
+"""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""
+
+- SERCOM0 to SERCOM3 only; no CAN, ICM, SMBIST, PTC. The MC00 adds SDADC,
+  TSENS and a second RTC version (U2250), which are generic register
+  blocks.
+- PORT has groups A and B (QOM properties ``pa-*`` and ``pb-*``). GCLK has
+  35 peripheral channels.
+- NVMCTRL has no ECC (no FLASHERR, FLTCAP, SERR or DERR flags).
+- DSU.DID is 0x11070X06: revision ``A2`` (1, default) or ``A1`` (0), set
+  with ``-global pic32cm1216mc00048-soc.silicon-rev=A1``.
+
+Board
+"""""
+
+``-serial`` options are connected to SERCOM0 (EDBG virtual COM port, PA06
+TX / PA07 RX) and SERCOM3 (EXT1/EXT2 USART, PA22/PA23), in that order.
+
+LED0 (PA24, active low) is a QEMU LED device; ``-trace led_set_intensity``
+shows it. User switch SW0 (PA25, to ground, no external pull-up) is the
+machine property ``sw0-pressed``, also settable at run time with
+``qom-set /machine sw0-pressed true``.
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+  $ qemu-system-arm -M pic32cm-mc00-cpro -kernel app.elf \
+      -display none -serial stdio -d unimp,guest_errors
